course: dictionary
lesson: 9905
title: One word, many uses: talking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word talking can do different jobs in a sentence. Look at the words around it to find out which job it does. «No talking during the test.» Here talking is a noun, the act of speaking, and the sign tells you not to do it.
explain: «She is talking to her friend about the film.» Here talking is a verb. It is the -ing form of talk, so it shows an action that is happening now. Ask yourself: is talking a doing word, a naming word, or a describing word in this sentence?
explain: «The talking parrot said hello to everyone.» Here talking is an adjective. It describes the parrot and tells you it can say words. Try swapping in your own meaning, "the parrot able to speak", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Talking is also used for feelings and safety. «Talking to a trusted adult» helps when you are worried. Sam used the phrase «a talking-to» to mean a telling-off, so always check the words around it before you decide what it means.
fact: Talking can be a verb, a noun, or an adjective.
fact: As a verb, talking means saying words to people, the -ing form of talk: talk, talks, talked, talking.
fact: As a noun, talking means the act of speaking, as in «No talking in the library».
fact: As an adjective, talking means able to talk, as in «a talking doll» or «a talking animal in a story».
fact: A talking-to is a telling-off, and talking point means something people want to discuss.
exercise: «No talking during the test.» What does talking mean in this sentence? | Writing neatly | Reading quietly | *The act of speaking | A kind of bird
exercise: «A talking parrot» is a parrot that can do what? | Sing a song | Fly very high | Sleep all day | *Say words
exercise: Sam asks, «Why do boys who fight get a detention, but girls who fight just get a talking-to?» What is a talking-to? | *A telling-off | A list of rules | A lesson about speaking clearly | A friendly chat about hobbies
test: In «a talking doll», what kind of word is talking? | A noun | A pronoun | A verb | *An adjective
test: If you are worried, who is a good person to start talking to? | Your toy | *A trusted adult | A stranger online | Nobody, keep it inside
exam: Which sentence uses talking as a noun? | «We are talking about the ideas.» | «Stop talking now, please.» | «The talking parrot sang loudly.» | *«No talking in the library.»
